  "body": "Sibling of magpie-community/plugins@ba9801c (trae 0.2.21), which fixed a Trae CN check-in shown as 200 credits when the account got 100 (zhujiu on Discord, 10-25). The plugin added the status's `credits` and `extra_credits`; a real status carries both at 100 (#808), and the real claim names no credit (`{\"code\":0,\"message\":\"success\"}`, plugins#194).\n\nmagpie's own Go check-in, `traeCheckin` in `internal/provider/trae_checkin.go`, runs only for a Trae CN plugin before 0.2.17 (`traeCheckinAccounts` returns nothing once `pluginChecksIn`). Its fallback already takes the status's `credits` alone, so the real answers give 100. But it still returns `credit + got.ExtraCredits`: a claim naming both `credits` and `extra_credits` would show their sum. No real claim has been seen with either field, so this is not known to show a wrong number today. The plugin now takes `credits`, else `extra_credits` alone, never both; the Go path should match, or be removed once no supported plugin version needs it.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
