   "body": "Delivered on `fix/trae-checkin-credits` ([0a2a0d74](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/0a2a0d74), skygunner's fork, on upstream/main 641b1217): the Go check-in's fallback takes the claim's credits, else its extra_credits, else the status's count as before — never their sum, matching what trae 0.2.21's plugin took (magpie-community/plugins@ba9801c) after the 200-shown-for-100 report.\n\nRed before (`TestTraeCheckinTakesOneCreditNotTheirSum`, on synthetic claims): a claim of both at 100 showed 200, and a claim of extra_credits 50 alone showed 150; after, 100 and 50, a claim of credits 80 shows 80, and a claim naming neither keeps the status's 100. Every other Trae check-in answer is unchanged, and the path runs only for a Trae CN plugin older than 0.2.17 (`traeCheckinAccounts` returns nothing once `pluginChecksIn`), so no supported plugin takes it.\n\nOne honesty note, as the issue says: no real claim has been seen naming either field (plugins#194), so this is the protocol kept right on synthetic fixture answers — no live incident is claimed fixed.\n\nRun: `go test ./internal/provider -count=1` (ok), gofmt, go vet, windows/amd64 and darwin/arm64 builds.",
